{
  "id": "7-20-quest-3-lab-duel-a-classmate",
  "title": "7.20.3 Lab: Duel a classmate",
  "description": "H hosts a duel, Red against Blue, with a classmate on another computer: a choice sends { act, roll }, act runs in onMove only for the seat whose turn it is and only for a good move, and the campaign still plays offline.",
  "type": "lesson",
  "estimateMins": 25,
  "category": "Unit 2: moSHion: Applied Game Development",
  "unit": "7.20 Quest: duel online",
  "preview": "moshion",
  "week": 19,
  "slos": [
    "SLO-3"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "title": "Run it",
      "instructions": "This is your game from 7.19.3. It plays on one computer; H does nothing yet.",
      "hints": [
        "If you brought your 7.19.3 work forward, your names may differ; keep yours. Where a step quotes a line, change the line of yours that does the same job."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "title": "A duel flag, and Red against Blue",
      "instructions": "At the top, below the comment lines, add `const JOIN = '';`. Below `let over = false;`, add `let duel = false;`. In `newGame()`, put the three lines that make the enemies and the fighters inside the `else` of an `if (duel)`: `if (duel) { fighters = [new Fighter('Red', 30, 3, 2, 'tomato'), new Fighter('Blue', 30, 3, 2, 'dodgerblue')]; } else { ...your three lines... }`. Change the first message to `message = duel ? 'Red goes first: 1 attack, 2 guard, 3 potion' : 'Your turn: 1 attack, 2 guard, 3 potion';`. Run: the campaign plays as before, because `duel` is false.",
      "hints": [
        "Red and Blue get the same numbers, so the duel is a fair fight."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "title": "A room and a listener",
      "instructions": "At the end of `setup()`, apply every move that arrives: `online.onMove((m, seat) => { if (duel && !over) act(turn, m.act, m.roll); });`. Below it, join a room when there is a code: `if (JOIN !== '') { duel = true; newGame(); online.join(JOIN); }`. In `draw()`, below `background(...)`, H hosts a duel: `if (kb.presses('h') && !duel && online.status === 'off') { duel = true; newGame(); online.host(); }`. Run: the campaign plays as before. (H now opens a room, but the top does not show it yet.)",
      "hints": [
        "Without `newGame()`, the hurt hero from your campaign would be in the duel on your computer, while your classmate's starts fresh, and the two would never match.",
        "The next steps send the moves, and check each one before `act` runs it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "title": "Send the move, do not make it",
      "instructions": "In `choose(a)`, roll first, then send or act: `const roll = floor(random(0, 4));`, then `if (duel) online.send({ act: a, roll: roll });` and `else act(turn, a, roll);`. In `act`, the computer enemy only plays when this is not a duel: change `if (turn === 1) after(45, enemyTurn);` to `if (!duel && turn === 1) after(45, enemyTurn);`. At the very top of `fightOver(winner)`: `if (duel) { over = true; message = fighters[winner].name + ' wins the duel!'; return; }`. Run: the campaign still plays, because `duel` is false.",
      "hints": [
        "The sender rolls, once, and sends the roll: then both computers use the same roll, and the hp bars agree.",
        "Online, an action done where you press the key AND in `onMove` would happen twice on your screen."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "title": "Check every move that arrives",
      "instructions": "Below `newGame()`, add the check from the reading: `function goodMove(m) { return m !== null && typeof m === 'object' && [1, 2, 3].includes(m.act) && [0, 1, 2, 3].includes(m.roll); }`. Then make `onMove` check before it acts: change its line to `if (duel && !over && seat === turn && goodMove(m)) act(turn, m.act, m.roll);`. Run: the campaign plays as before.",
      "hints": [
        "A move like `{ act: '1', roll: 0 }` holds the word '1', not the number 1, so `goodMove` ignores it on both computers. So does a roll of 99.",
        "`seat === turn` ignores a move sent by the player whose turn it is not."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "title": "Only your seat chooses",
      "instructions": "Below `goodMove`, add `myTurn()`: `function myTurn() { if (!duel) return turn === 0; return online.status === 'ready' && online.seat === turn; }`. In `draw()`, the key block starts with `if (!over && myTurn())` instead of `if (!over && turn === 0)`. R only works offline: change the R line to `if (kb.presses('r') && over && !duel) newGame();`. Run: the campaign plays, and after a win or a loss R starts it again.",
      "hints": [
        "Seat 0 is the host and plays Red, `fighters[0]`; seat 1 is the classmate and plays Blue."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "title": "Show the room",
      "instructions": "In `drawTop()`, the Fight line is only for the campaign: change it to `if (!duel) text('Fight ' + (which + 1) + ' of ' + enemies.length + '    H: duel a classmate', 10, 46, 12, '#8393c4');`. Below it, add these lines, one for each thing the room can be doing:\n\n- `if (duel && online.status === 'connecting') text('Connecting to the room...', 10, 46, 12, 'gold');`\n- `if (duel && online.status === 'waiting') text('Room code: ' + online.code, 10, 50, 18, 'gold');`\n- `if (duel && online.status === 'ready' && !over && online.seat < 2) text('Online duel: you are ' + fighters[online.seat].name + '. Turn: ' + fighters[turn].name, 10, 46, 12, 'gold');`\n- `if (duel && online.status === 'ready' && !over && online.seat > 1) text('You are watching. Turn: ' + fighters[turn].name, 10, 46, 12, 'gold');`\n- `if (duel && online.status === 'ready' && over) text('Play again: Stop, Run. One hosts (H), one joins the new code', 10, 46, 12, 'gold');`\n- `if (duel && online.status === 'closed') text('Room closed: one hosts (H), one joins the new code', 10, 46, 12, 'gold');`\n- `if (duel && online.status === 'error') text(('' + online.error).slice(0, 60), 10, 46, 12, 'tomato');`\n\nRun and press H: the top shows `Room code:` and six letters, big enough to read out.",
      "hints": [
        "The canvas is 480 pixels wide: keep each line short, and start them near the left edge.",
        "Only seats 0 and 1 have a fighter. `online.seat < 2` keeps the first ready line from asking for `fighters[2]`, which does not exist, if a third player ever gets in.",
        "When the duel is over, the turn line is hidden: the message above already says who won."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "title": "Duel a classmate",
      "instructions": "Host in one tab: press H and read the code. In a second tab (or on a classmate's computer), put that code in `JOIN`, for example `const JOIN = 'K7QX2M';`, and Run. Both tops now say Online duel. Play to a win.\n\n**To duel again:** press Stop, then Run, in both tabs. Only ONE player presses H; the other puts the NEW code in `JOIN` and runs again. If both press H, you are in two different rooms. Running again with the OLD code joins the old room and shows the finished duel again: only a new code starts a new duel.\n\n**When you are done:** set `JOIN` back to `''`. 7.21.3 starts from this code, and a code left in `JOIN` would join the old duel instead of starting the campaign.",
      "hints": [
        "You must be signed in and in a class to play online.",
        "Press a key when it is not your turn: nothing happens, on either computer."
      ]
    }
  ],
